           <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-text mb-3">11. Security</h2>
           <p>The Software employs the following defensive practices:</p>
           <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 list-disc list-outside ml-5">
-            <li><strong class="text-text">Local secret encryption.</strong> AI Chat API keys, git access tokens, certificate passphrases and keystore passwords, saved keystores, one-time-password secrets, and credential-named settings such as a proxy password are encrypted at rest via Electron <code class="text-xs bg-bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">safeStorage</code>, which delegates to the OS keychain. If the keychain is unavailable on your system, AI Chat keys and remembered keystore passwords are not saved at all; the other values are then stored without encryption. Secret-type variables, mock server tokens and passwords, and credentials typed into an Auth tab are <strong class="text-text">not</strong> encrypted at rest: they sit in the local database as plain text, and are blanked in project files, git and exports (Section 3).</li>
+            <li><strong class="text-text">Local secret encryption.</strong> AI Chat API keys, git access tokens, certificate passphrases and keystore passwords, saved keystores, one-time-password secrets, and credential-named settings such as a proxy password are encrypted at rest via Electron <code class="text-xs bg-bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">safeStorage</code>, which delegates to the OS keychain. If the keychain is unavailable on your system, AI Chat keys and remembered keystore passwords are not saved at all; the other values are then stored without encryption. Secret-type variables, mock server tokens, passwords and API keys, and Mock MCP bearer tokens are encrypted the same way (stored without encryption while the keychain is unavailable, and encrypted on a later launch once it is), and are blanked in project files, git and exports (Section 3). Credentials typed into an Auth tab are <strong class="text-text">not</strong> encrypted at rest: they sit in the local database as plain text.</li>
             <li><strong class="text-text">No stream messages on disk.</strong> The messages and events received over SSE, WebSocket and Socket.IO, and MCP notifications, are kept in memory only and are not written to disk; History records the connection, not the messages (Section 3). MCP tool, resource and prompt results are recorded in History, masked.</li>
             <li><strong class="text-text">Renderer hardening.</strong> The Renderer process runs with <code class="text-xs bg-bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">contextIsolation: true</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">nodeIntegration: false</code>, and a strict CSP of <code class="text-xs bg-bg-muted px-1 py-0.5 rounded">connect-src 'self'</code>, which means the UI cannot make outbound network calls.</li>
             <li><strong class="text-text">Process separation.</strong> The UI cannot directly access the filesystem, child processes, or network. All such operations are mediated by typed IPC channels with input validation in the Main process.</li>
